I agree with lojbab, "be careful" is probably an English idiom. French uses
"fais attention =E0..." which is essentially "pay attention to..."; a nativ=
e
francophone might consider {jundi} first.

I'd suggest {.i .o'i lo nu <condition> ka'e jai ri'a cortu} where
<condition> is whatever will make the toy hurt the baby.
Or, if you don't care about the condition exactly, {tu'a lo selkei ka'e jai
ri'a cortu} or {lo selkei ka'e jai jai ri'a cortu}

Then again, do you use weirdo grammar like {ka'e jai ri'a} when talking to
babies?

mu'o mi'e la tsani

